The legal text is the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia (English translation compiled by the Secretariat General of the Senate, March 2008),
hosted by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Cambodia (mfaic.gov.kh). The bytes were read from the Internet Archive capture of 2 November 2021.

The Constitution and translations of it are not protected by copyright in Cambodia. Law on Copyright and Related Rights (2003), Article 10:
  "The following works shall not be fallen under any protection by this law:
   a- Constitution, Law, Royal Decree, Sub-Decree, and other Regulations.
   ...
   d- Translation of those materials mentioned in the preceding paragraphs (a), (b), and (c) of this article."

Changes made by Lexifina: the PDF's line wraps were joined into one paragraph per line and the text was divided into one file per article.
The wording was not changed. Neither the Senate nor the Ministry endorses this repository.

The treaty facts are taken from the United Nations Treaty Collection (https://treaties.un.org/), retrieved 30 October 2026:
treaty names, kinds of action and dates only. The Treaty Collection's robots.txt (Crawl-delay: 2) was obeyed.

The legal-system facts are from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org/), released under CC0 1.0 Universal.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
